# S — systems: the Endowment has no staff and publishes no stack. What can be seen is its website (the file paths under /wp-content/ show it runs on WordPress) and, behind the
# giving flows, the Foundation's fundraising systems, which belong to atom/wikimedia-foundation.
nodes:
  - id: S:system/endowment-site
    type: system
    name: The Endowment's website
    summary: wikimediaendowment.org, which the file paths of its uploads suggest runs on WordPress; maintained by Foundation staff under the cost-sharing agreement.
    category: website
    vendor: none
    counterparty: none
    regulatory-criticality: low
    used-by: [P:offering/legacy-giving, P:offering/project-grants, P:offering/permanent-fund]
    admin: O:position/president
    status: active
    visibility: public
    owner: O:role/president
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ["https://wikimediaendowment.org/", "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/foundation/d/df/FY2627-Endowment_Annual_Plan.pdf"], confidence: 0.5, state: known}
    pending: "what the site runs on and who administers it (inferred from upload paths; not stated)"
    replacement: none
